// Title: Rundll32 Execution Without CommandLine Parameters
// Sigma ID: 1775e15e-b61b-4d14-a1a3-80981298085a
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-05-27 | Modified: 2023-08-31
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1202
// Description: Detects suspicious start of rundll32.exe without any parameters as found in CobaltStrike beacon
//   activity
// False positives:
//   - Possible but rare
// References:
//   - https://www.cobaltstrike.com/help-opsec
//   - https://twitter.com/ber_m1ng/status/1397948048135778309
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_rundll32_no_params.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or ProcessCommandLine endswith "\\rundll32.exe\"" or ProcessCommandLine endswith "\\rundll32") and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\AppData\\Local\\" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\Microsoft\\Edge\\")))
